# The committed `.pre-commit-config.yaml` is the portable form of the MCL
# Standard Hook Set (metacraft-dev-guidelines repo-requirements.md 4.1-4.3),
# so it must NOT be ignored. The entry that used to ignore it here as a
# "Nix-generated" file is stale, measured rather than assumed: `git grep -ni
# pre-commit -- '*.nix'` matches nothing in this repository, this fork's
# flake.nix takes only nixpkgs as an input and wires no git hooks, and a
# checkout of this fork carries no `.pre-commit-config.yaml` symlink into
# /nix/store (8 workspace repos do; this is not one of them).
#
# An ignored config is a trap, not a nicety: plain `git add` of it is refused,
# so a hook set can be installed, pass its own proofs locally, and never be
# committed at all -- which is exactly how a gate ends up existing on one
# machine. These two lines were Metacraft's and not upstream's (nim-lang/Nim
# devel carries no pre-commit entry in .gitignore), so replacing them conflicts
# with nothing upstream maintains.
!.pre-commit-config.yaml

# Repro development environment cache
.repro/

# The fork writes macro_sourcemap_<name>.json into the nimcache; older builds
# of it wrote the file beside the output binary, often inside a source tree.
macro_sourcemap_*.json
